This currently throws an error:

```bash
/Users/samc/work/zod-openapi-2/node_modules/.pnpm/@zod+core@0.3.3/node_modules/@zod/core/dist/commonjs/registries.js:18
                throw new Error(`ID ${meta.id} already exists in the registry`);
                      ^

Error: ID jobId already exists in the registry
```

Which I don't believe is the most intuitive behaviour?

The alternative would be

```ts
console.log(
  JSON.stringify(
    z.toJSONSchema(
      z.object({
        current: baseJobId,
        previous: baseJobId.meta({ description: "previous job id" }),
      }),
      {
        reused: "ref",
      }
    ),
    null,
    2
  )
