## Goal
`packages/mcp`'s two duplicated `normalizePlatform`/`normalizeRegistryPlatform` implementations should return an empty value for unrecognized platform input, matching the canonical `packages/registry/src/platforms-lib.js#normalizePlatform` contract, instead of leaking the raw unrecognized string back out.

## Why this matters
The registry package's `normalizePlatform` returns `undefined` for any value not in `PLATFORM_ALIASES` — callers treat that as "no valid platform, don't filter." The MCP package has two independent mirrors of this function (`packages/mcp/src/registry-normalize-lib.js#normalizePlatform` and `packages/mcp/src/search-ranking-lib.js#normalizeRegistryPlatform`) that both fall back to `String(value || "").trim()` instead of an empty/undefined value, so an unrecognized platform string is returned verbatim rather than treated as "unknown."

This directly breaks platform filtering: `matchesRegistryPlatform` (`search-ranking-lib.js`) does `const target = normalizeRegistryPlatform(platform); if (!target) return true;` — the intended behavior for an invalid/misspelled platform is "no filter, match everything," but because the fallback is never falsy for non-empty input, a typo'd or garbage platform string becomes a strict-equality filter against canonical `entry.platforms` values it can never match. Every MCP tool that filters by platform (`search_registry`, `plan_workflow_toolbox`, compare/trust-compare/safety-review handlers in `registry-tool-orchestration-lib.js`) silently returns zero results for a misspelled platform instead of ignoring the bad filter, and echoes the garbage string back in tool responses as if it were an accepted platform value.

Verified with a direct repro:
```
node -e "console.log(require('./packages/registry/src/platforms-lib.js').normalizePlatform('Cluade Code'))"
// undefined
node -e "console.log(require('./packages/mcp/src/registry-normalize-lib.js').normalizePlatform('Cluade Code'))"
// "Cluade Code"  <- leaked verbatim
```

## Current behavior
`packages/mcp/src/registry-normalize-lib.js` (`normalizePlatform`, ~line 51-55):
```js
export function normalizePlatform(value) {
  const normalized = normalizeText(value).replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, "-");
  if (!normalized) return "";
  return platformAliases.get(normalized) || String(value || "").trim();
}
```
`packages/mcp/src/search-ranking-lib.js` (`normalizeRegistryPlatform`, ~line 340-344) has the identical bug:
```js
export function normalizeRegistryPlatform(value) {
  const normalized = text(value).replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, "-");
  if (!normalized) return "";
  return PLATFORM_ALIASES.get(normalized) || String(value || "").trim();
}
```
Compare `packages/registry/src/platforms-lib.js` (`normalizePlatform`, ~line 72-78):
```js
export function normalizePlatform(value) {
  if (typeof value !== "string") return undefined;
  const key = value.trim().toLowerCase();
  return Object.hasOwn(PLATFORM_ALIASES, key) ? PLATFORM_ALIASES[key] : undefined;
}
```

