### Component

src / feeds (`src/feeds.mjs`)

### Description

The coverage-delta feed item in `registryItems` renders the absent side as the literal string `undefined` when `changelog.summary.coverage_delta` carries only one of `surface_count` / `candidate_count`:

```js
const surfaceDelta = cov?.surface_count?.delta || 0;
const candidateDelta = cov?.candidate_count?.delta || 0;
if (surfaceDelta || candidateDelta) {
  ...
  title: `Coverage updated: ${sign(surfaceDelta)} surfaces, ${sign(candidateDelta)} candidates`,
  summary: clamp(
    `Surfaces ${cov.surface_count?.before}→${cov.surface_count?.after}; ` +
      `candidates ${cov.candidate_count?.before}→${cov.candidate_count?.after}.`,
  ),
```

When only one side is present, the block still enters (the other delta is non-zero), and the absent side interpolates `undefined`.

#### Where

`src/feeds.mjs`, `registryItems` (the `coverage_delta` item).

#### Reproduction

`registryItems({ summary: { coverage_delta: { candidate_count: { before: 50, after: 49, delta: -1 } } } })` yields:

- title: `"Coverage updated: +0 surfaces, -1 candidates"` (misleading `+0 surfaces` — there was no surface delta at all)
- summary: `"Surfaces undefined→undefined; candidates 50→49."`

#### Impact

Garbage text (`undefined→undefined`) and a misleading `+0 surfaces` in the live registry feed (`/api/v1/feeds/registry`) whenever a coverage refresh reports only one of the two counts.

#### Proposed fix

Build the title and summary from only the side(s) actually present:

```js
const titleParts = [];
const summaryParts = [];
if (cov?.surface_count) {
  titleParts.push(`${sign(surfaceDelta)} surfaces`);
  summaryParts.push(`Surfaces ${cov.surface_count.before}→${cov.surface_count.after}`);
}
if (cov?.candidate_count) {
  titleParts.push(`${sign(candidateDelta)} candidates`);
  summaryParts.push(`candidates ${cov.candidate_count.before}→${cov.candidate_count.after}`);
}
// title: `Coverage updated: ${titleParts.join(", ")}`, summary: clamp(`${summaryParts.join("; ")}.`)
```

The both-present output is byte-for-byte unchanged. Add a regression test for the candidate-only partial delta.

