In `crates/engine/src/game/layers.rs`, layer-7 continuous-effect evaluation applies power/toughness **counters** *after* the power/toughness **switch** effect, which is the reverse of the order the Comprehensive Rules require.

The layer loop explicitly skips `Layer::CounterPT` and applies counter P/T deltas in a separate pass that runs **after** the loop completes:

```rust
// crates/engine/src/game/layers.rs:1114  (full evaluation)
for (layer, layer_bucket) in &effects_by_layer {
    if matches!(*layer, Layer::Copy | Layer::CounterPT) {
        // Copy handled above; Counter-based P/T handled separately below.
        continue;
    }
    ...
    for effect in &ordered {
        apply_continuous_effect(state, effect);   // <- SwitchPT (Layer 7d) applied HERE, in the loop
    }
}
...
// crates/engine/src/game/layers.rs:1190
// CR 613.4c: Power/toughness counters modify P/T in layer 7c.
for &id in &bf_ids {                              // <- counters applied HERE, AFTER the loop
    ... obj.power += power_delta; obj.toughness += toughness_delta; ...
