### Describe the bug

At runtime, `@trpc/server` converts `IncomingMessage` to `Request`, and as part of the conversion, it has to map the headers as well (see line 70 below)...
https://github.com/trpc/trpc/blob/38b26761f0378fa7f1e937fe14d5dd01b7a42df5/packages/server/src/adapters/node-http/incomingMessageToRequest.ts#L58-L71


I have a http2 server in fastify, (but I assume that this issue will impact all http2 server implementations).
http2 headers include pseudo-headers which start with a colon ( `:`), such as `:method`, `:path`, etc

The http2 pseudo-headers cause problems, because, `new Headers()` does not accept header names that start with `:`. Therefore, we should not directly pass in the headers, but filter out http2 headers first

