The local `let _child` (derived from the user's loop variable name `child` with the `_` prefix) shadows the imported `child` helper (aliased `_child`) within the same function scope, so the earlier `_child(n29)` call hits the temporal dead zone.

Renaming the loop variable (e.g. `v-for="sub in items"`) makes the component work — which also means any codebase using the very common name `child` in a v-for crashes under Vapor.

Likely fix: codegen should reserve/uniquify cache identifiers against the helper alias set (same class of problem as #14296, but for v-for item cache vs runtime helper imports).

